{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-atom-knot-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:atom-knot-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the atom-knot for any (Z, N)","tags":["existence","atom-knot","borromean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomKnot.exists","text":"atom-knot-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/atom-knot-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:atom-knot-exists\"></a><p><em>For any pair <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(Z, N) \\in \\mathbb{N}_{\\geq 0}^2</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z + N \\geq 1</code>, the atom-knot of type <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(Z, N)</code> exists as a closed braid in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_{3(Z+N)}(q)</code> on the generic locus.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/atom-knot-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.10.2"}
